1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,380
Today your scripts earn trust, because you will test them.

2
00:00:03,930 --> 00:00:06,260
A script that works once proves little.

3
00:00:06,260 --> 00:00:09,127
A test proves it still works after every change.

4
00:00:09,127 --> 00:00:12,472
And a mock lets you test code that talks to the network,

5
00:00:12,472 --> 00:00:14,085
without any network at all.

6
00:00:14,635 --> 00:00:17,920
Every demo is typed live on Ubuntu twenty-four oh four.

7
00:00:19,970 --> 00:00:21,966
Every change can break something.

8
00:00:21,966 --> 00:00:25,052
A test is a small script that checks one behaviour,

9
00:00:25,052 --> 00:00:27,714
and fails loudly when that behaviour breaks.

10
00:00:28,264 --> 00:00:30,280
Pytest finds files named test,

11
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:31,019
underscore,

12
00:00:31,019 --> 00:00:31,691
something.

13
00:00:31,691 --> 00:00:33,908
It runs the functions named test,

14
00:00:33,908 --> 00:00:34,647
underscore,

15
00:00:34,647 --> 00:00:35,319
something,

16
00:00:35,319 --> 00:00:37,939
and it uses the plain assert statement.

17
00:00:37,939 --> 00:00:38,678
No classes,

18
00:00:38,678 --> 00:00:39,955
and no boilerplate.

19
00:00:40,505 --> 00:00:43,294
Parametrize runs one test with many inputs.

20
00:00:43,294 --> 00:00:46,798
Pytest dot raises checks that the right error happens.

21
00:00:47,348 --> 00:00:48,751
A mock is a stand-in.

22
00:00:48,751 --> 00:00:50,554
Our code calls the network,

23
00:00:50,554 --> 00:00:52,158
but a test must be fast,

24
00:00:52,158 --> 00:00:52,492
free,

25
00:00:52,492 --> 00:00:53,494
and repeatable.

26
00:00:53,494 --> 00:00:56,834
So we replace the network call with a fake answer,

27
00:00:56,834 --> 00:00:58,036
or a fake failure.

28
00:00:58,586 --> 00:01:00,371
The rule: test one behaviour,

29
00:01:00,371 --> 00:01:02,157
fake what you do not control,

30
00:01:02,157 --> 00:01:04,065
and watch every test fail once,

31
00:01:04,065 --> 00:01:05,050
to prove it can.

32
00:01:07,100 --> 00:01:11,921
First, the code we will test. Show it. Type: cat, inventory dot P Y.

33
00:01:12,771 --> 00:01:14,187
Two small functions.

34
00:01:14,187 --> 00:01:17,656
Running returns the names of the running servers.

35
00:01:17,656 --> 00:01:20,983
Health calls an address and returns its status.

36
00:01:20,983 --> 00:01:22,541
First we test running.

37
00:01:22,541 --> 00:01:23,886
Show the test file.

38
00:01:23,886 --> 00:01:24,594
Type: cat,

39
00:01:24,594 --> 00:01:27,001
test underscore inventory dot P Y.

40
00:01:27,551 --> 00:01:28,383
Three tests.

41
00:01:28,383 --> 00:01:31,641
Each is a function whose name starts with test,

42
00:01:31,641 --> 00:01:33,860
and the check is a plain assert.

43
00:01:33,860 --> 00:01:36,356
Parametrize runs the last one twice,

44
00:01:36,356 --> 00:01:38,159
with two different states.

45
00:01:38,159 --> 00:01:38,921
Run pytest.

46
00:01:38,921 --> 00:01:39,823
Type: pytest,

47
00:01:39,823 --> 00:01:40,308
dash Q.

48
00:01:41,358 --> 00:01:42,081
Four dots,

49
00:01:42,081 --> 00:01:42,948
four passed.

50
00:01:42,948 --> 00:01:44,466
Each dot is one test.

51
00:01:44,466 --> 00:01:45,478
Green is good,

52
00:01:45,478 --> 00:01:48,803
but a test that can never fail proves nothing.

53
00:01:48,803 --> 00:01:50,466
So break it on purpose.

54
00:01:50,466 --> 00:01:53,285
Change the expected name on line eight.

55
00:01:53,285 --> 00:01:54,008
Type: sed,

56
00:01:54,008 --> 00:01:54,514
dash I,

57
00:01:54,514 --> 00:01:54,947
quote,

58
00:01:54,947 --> 00:01:55,381
eight,

59
00:01:55,381 --> 00:01:55,959
S slash,

60
00:01:55,959 --> 00:01:57,260
web dash zero one,

61
00:01:57,260 --> 00:01:57,694
slash,

62
00:01:57,694 --> 00:01:59,068
web dash zero nine,

63
00:01:59,068 --> 00:01:59,501
slash,

64
00:01:59,501 --> 00:01:59,935
quote,

65
00:01:59,935 --> 00:02:02,393
test underscore inventory dot P Y.

66
00:02:02,943 --> 00:02:03,686
No output,

67
00:02:03,686 --> 00:02:05,173
the file is changed.

68
00:02:05,173 --> 00:02:06,659
Run the tests again,

69
00:02:06,659 --> 00:02:08,964
with the short traceback style.

70
00:02:08,964 --> 00:02:09,930
Type: pytest,

71
00:02:09,930 --> 00:02:10,450
dash Q,

72
00:02:10,450 --> 00:02:11,491
dash dash T B,

73
00:02:11,491 --> 00:02:12,011
equals,

74
00:02:12,011 --> 00:02:12,457
short.

75
00:02:13,507 --> 00:02:13,935
One F,

76
00:02:13,935 --> 00:02:14,791
one failure.

77
00:02:14,791 --> 00:02:16,931
Pytest shows the failing line,

78
00:02:16,931 --> 00:02:20,282
and compares the two values: web dash zero one,

79
00:02:20,282 --> 00:02:22,208
against web dash zero nine.

80
00:02:22,208 --> 00:02:24,133
The summary names the test,

81
00:02:24,133 --> 00:02:25,988
so you know where to look.

82
00:02:25,988 --> 00:02:26,772
Now fix it.

83
00:02:26,772 --> 00:02:27,485
Type: sed,

84
00:02:27,485 --> 00:02:27,985
dash I,

85
00:02:27,985 --> 00:02:28,412
quote,

86
00:02:28,412 --> 00:02:28,840
eight,

87
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:29,411
S slash,

88
00:02:29,411 --> 00:02:30,766
web dash zero nine,

89
00:02:30,766 --> 00:02:31,194
slash,

90
00:02:31,194 --> 00:02:32,477
web dash zero one,

91
00:02:32,477 --> 00:02:32,905
slash,

92
00:02:32,905 --> 00:02:33,333
quote,

93
00:02:33,333 --> 00:02:35,758
test underscore inventory dot P Y.

94
00:02:36,308 --> 00:02:40,105
Fixed. Run everything once more. Type: pytest, dash Q.

95
00:02:41,155 --> 00:02:42,233
Four passed again.

96
00:02:42,233 --> 00:02:42,831
That loop,

97
00:02:42,831 --> 00:02:43,729
red then green,

98
00:02:43,729 --> 00:02:46,003
is the heart of testing: write a test,

99
00:02:46,003 --> 00:02:46,841
watch it fail,

100
00:02:46,841 --> 00:02:47,918
then make it pass.

101
00:02:49,968 --> 00:02:51,210
Now the hard case.

102
00:02:51,210 --> 00:02:52,936
Health calls the network,

103
00:02:52,936 --> 00:02:56,387
and a test must never depend on a server being up.

104
00:02:56,387 --> 00:02:57,905
So we fake the answer.

105
00:02:57,905 --> 00:02:58,872
Show the test.

106
00:02:58,872 --> 00:02:59,562
Type: cat,

107
00:02:59,562 --> 00:03:01,701
test underscore health dot P Y.

108
00:03:02,251 --> 00:03:03,872
Mock makes a fake object,

109
00:03:03,872 --> 00:03:06,725
and we tell it what its json method returns.

110
00:03:06,725 --> 00:03:08,605
Patch swaps requests dot get,

111
00:03:08,605 --> 00:03:09,772
inside our module,

112
00:03:09,772 --> 00:03:10,615
for the fake,

113
00:03:10,615 --> 00:03:12,365
only inside the with block.

114
00:03:12,365 --> 00:03:15,866
In the second test the fake raises a connection error,

115
00:03:15,866 --> 00:03:19,692
and pytest dot raises checks that our code lets it through.

116
00:03:19,692 --> 00:03:20,859
Run all the tests.

117
00:03:20,859 --> 00:03:21,701
Type: pytest,

118
00:03:21,701 --> 00:03:22,155
dash Q.

119
00:03:23,205 --> 00:03:23,983
Six passed,

120
00:03:23,983 --> 00:03:26,103
with no network and no server,

121
00:03:26,103 --> 00:03:27,941
in a fraction of a second.

122
00:03:27,941 --> 00:03:29,920
Now list every test by name.

123
00:03:29,920 --> 00:03:30,839
Type: pytest,

124
00:03:30,839 --> 00:03:31,333
dash V.

125
00:03:32,383 --> 00:03:35,742
Verbose mode shows each test with the word passed.

126
00:03:35,742 --> 00:03:38,764
Handy when you need to know exactly what ran.

127
00:03:38,764 --> 00:03:40,980
You can also run just some tests,

128
00:03:40,980 --> 00:03:42,458
by a word in the name.

129
00:03:42,458 --> 00:03:43,331
Type: pytest,

130
00:03:43,331 --> 00:03:43,801
dash Q,

131
00:03:43,801 --> 00:03:44,272
dash K,

132
00:03:44,272 --> 00:03:44,607
down.

133
00:03:45,657 --> 00:03:46,459
One passed,

134
00:03:46,459 --> 00:03:47,626
five deselected.

135
00:03:47,626 --> 00:03:48,939
And in a pipeline,

136
00:03:48,939 --> 00:03:52,803
pytest returns exit code zero when everything passes,

137
00:03:52,803 --> 00:03:55,720
and a non zero code when anything fails,

138
00:03:55,720 --> 00:03:57,324
so the pipeline stops.

139
00:03:57,324 --> 00:04:00,313
That is last lesson's exit codes at work.

140
00:04:02,363 --> 00:04:03,448
Here is your task,

141
00:04:03,448 --> 00:04:04,956
with everything you need.

142
00:04:04,956 --> 00:04:06,885
The files are in the repository,

143
00:04:06,885 --> 00:04:08,272
and in the description.

144
00:04:08,822 --> 00:04:14,497
The repository is git hub dot com, slash it dash waves, slash dev ops dash A I.

145
00:04:15,047 --> 00:04:19,788
In the academy slash lesson fifty-three folder you will find the task file,

146
00:04:19,788 --> 00:04:20,989
the module to test,

147
00:04:20,989 --> 00:04:22,001
and the checker,

148
00:04:22,001 --> 00:04:23,644
check fifty-three dot S H.

149
00:04:24,194 --> 00:04:25,518
You write one file,

150
00:04:25,518 --> 00:04:26,841
test tools dot P Y,

151
00:04:26,841 --> 00:04:31,996
for a small module with two functions: one counts servers per environment,

152
00:04:31,996 --> 00:04:34,434
and one asks an API for its status.

153
00:04:34,984 --> 00:04:36,767
Write at least five tests.

154
00:04:36,767 --> 00:04:37,863
Use parametrize,

155
00:04:37,863 --> 00:04:39,371
use pytest dot raises,

156
00:04:39,371 --> 00:04:42,182
and fake the network with mock and patch.

157
00:04:42,182 --> 00:04:44,307
No test may need a real server.

158
00:04:44,857 --> 00:04:46,167
The checker is strict.

159
00:04:46,167 --> 00:04:48,668
It breaks the module three different ways,

160
00:04:48,668 --> 00:04:50,811
and your tests must catch every one.

161
00:04:50,811 --> 00:04:54,265
Do not open the solution file until you have really tried.

162
00:04:54,815 --> 00:04:58,484
The checker shows six pass lines. Write your results in a report.

163
00:05:00,534 --> 00:05:04,459
Here is how your work is judged. Six points, and you need all six.

164
00:05:05,009 --> 00:05:06,844
The checker shows six pass lines.

165
00:05:07,394 --> 00:05:09,677
At least five tests, and all of them pass.

166
00:05:10,227 --> 00:05:13,213
You use parametrize, and pytest dot raises.

167
00:05:13,763 --> 00:05:16,601
The network is faked, so no test needs a server.

168
00:05:17,151 --> 00:05:21,396
Your tests catch bugs: the checker breaks the code, and your tests must fail.

169
00:05:21,946 --> 00:05:25,359
The report is complete, and you worked in your own virtual machine.

170
00:05:25,909 --> 00:05:27,531
To pass, you need all six.

171
00:05:29,581 --> 00:05:32,418
Your turn, in your own Ubuntu virtual machine.

172
00:05:32,968 --> 00:05:36,872
One: get the lesson folder, and activate your virtual environment.

173
00:05:37,422 --> 00:05:41,177
Two: install pytest and requests in your virtual environment.

174
00:05:41,727 --> 00:05:45,163
Three: write test tools dot P Y with five tests,

175
00:05:45,163 --> 00:05:48,170
and use parametrize and pytest dot raises.

176
00:05:48,720 --> 00:05:54,480
Four: fake the network with mock and patch. Test an ok answer, and an H T T P error.

177
00:05:55,030 --> 00:05:58,507
Five: break the code yourself, and watch one of your tests fail.

178
00:05:59,057 --> 00:06:01,532
Six: run the checker, and write your report.

179
00:06:02,082 --> 00:06:03,916
Pause the video, and begin now.

180
00:06:19,466 --> 00:06:20,341
Quick check.

181
00:06:20,891 --> 00:06:22,811
How does pytest find your tests?

182
00:06:23,361 --> 00:06:24,683
What does a mock replace?

183
00:06:25,233 --> 00:06:27,452
Why should you watch a test fail at least once?

184
00:06:28,002 --> 00:06:31,031
What exit code does pytest return when a test fails?

185
00:06:31,581 --> 00:06:37,427
Objective covered: MC06-O07, tests with pytest and mocks.

186
